sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 1 of the command development pipeline (docs/reference/command-development-pipeline.mdx). Swamp owns the whole prep flow and its state; the Gateway only authorizes it: it admits each request, mints short-lived GitHub App tokens, passes them by vault key name, and records outcomes. An author agent drafts, a separate review agent checks, Swamp opens the PR as the Orbit App, and one of two modes (manual or automatic) decides when Swamp adds the PR to the merge queue. GitHub auto-merge is not used. No code changes in this stage.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 1 · prep a command
  %% kind: pipeline.1-prep
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=terminal pill=target tone=gray
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane NK icon=terminal pill=caller tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>authorizes only
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>owns flow · state
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>author · reviewer
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>PR · merge queue
  participant NK as Nick<br/>owner
  Note over GW: Admit the prep request<br/>one command
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - authorizes a prep request for one command
  %%> - records the operation, so the CLI and web show its state
  %%> - mints a short-lived GitHub App token for the flow
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Gateway only authorizes; Swamp owns the flow and all of its state
  GW->>SW: Start the prep flow<br/>token as vault key name
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the command and its family
  %%> - the vault key name of the token, never the token itself
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - the prep flow as a Swamp workflow; today the orchestrator starts the agents by hand
  SW->>VM: Draft the three files<br/>preparing-commands skill
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the author agent drafts the chart, the docs page and the verification cases in a task VM
  %%> - preparation changes no code
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - Swamp starting the task VM and the agent as part of the prep flow
  Note over VM: Read first<br/>Recall · page · chart · code
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Recall `resolve` for the command and its family, and `decisions` for the family; current decisions override older text
  %%> - reads the existing page, chart and old fixture; reads the code only to learn what exists, never as the target
  %%> - for a sibling of an approved command, starts from the sibling's chart, page and cases
  Note over VM: Draft the chart<br/>flow-tighten rules
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes `docs/cli/FAMILY/COMMAND.mmd`, the ideal flow, even where the code differs
  %%> - the main path uses required parameters only; each optional flag gets its own `opt` block
  %%> - uses role names and placeholders, never Node ids, task ids or hostnames
  %%> - shows the failure and cleanup contract: what a failure leaves behind, what a rerun does
  Note over VM: Draft the docs page<br/>description · usage · errors
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes `docs/cli/FAMILY/COMMAND.mdx` in this order: description, usage, how it works, errors
  %%> - states the rerun behavior, with the reason code of a skip
  Note over VM: Draft the cases<br/>one row per case
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes `swamp/proof/FAMILY/COMMAND.cases.md` from the chart and the page, never from the code
  %%> - covers required arguments only, each flag, each error on the chart, a repeat, and a failure after a partial change
  %%> - marks a case that the code fails today; never weakens a case to fit the code
  Note over VM: Check the draft<br/>bin/check-flows · docs lint
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs `bin/check-flows`, `composer docs-build` and `composer docs-lint`
  %%> - walks every error code, flag and repeat of the page against the cases
  loop until the review has no findings
    SW->>VM: Review the drafts<br/>fresh read-only agent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a separate review agent (Sonnet, high effort) checks the drafts against the skills and the CLI standard
    %%> - it never wrote the drafts
    VM-->>SW: Findings<br/>or none
    SW->>VM: Fix the findings<br/>author agent
    %%> When:
    %%> - only when the review has findings
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the author agent fixes every finding it can settle with the rules and Recall decisions
  end
  SW->>GH: Open one docs-only PR<br/>as the Orbit App
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the token from the vault by its key name
  %%> - marks the chart `%% status: reviewed`
  %%> - the PR holds the chart, page and cases of one command and nothing else
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - PRs opened by the App from the prep flow; the Gateway already opens task PRs as the App with `tasks:publish`, but today the prep author opens this PR as `nckrtl`
  Note over GH: Docs checks only<br/>no VM job
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a documentation-only change runs the docs checks of CI and never the proof CI
  alt manual mode
    opt Nick reviews in an Instance
      NK->>GW: Create an Instance<br/>instance:create --branch=BRANCH
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - creates a development Instance that checks out the PR branch
      %%> - Nick and an agent review and adjust the drafts there
      %%> - a push moves the PR head, so the approval must follow the last push
      %%> Built or not:
      %%> - built: `instance:create --branch` checks out an existing origin branch (`docs/cli/instance/create.mdx`, Branch selection)
    end
    NK->>GH: Approve the exact head<br/>review in Nick's name
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - Nick asks the agent to post the approving review in his name
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the approval of the exact PR head is the gate; it is the only signal the flow waits for
    GW->>GH: Read the PR reviews<br/>short poll · approval on head
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the review decisions with a token that has only `pull_requests: read`
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the Gateway is private and its App receives no webhooks, so GitHub cannot call it; a short poll sees the approval
    %%> Built or not:
    %%> - built: the Gateway already reads review decisions this way for task pull requests
    %%> - not built: the approval-triggered continuation, which admits the next step of the prep flow
    GH-->>GW: Approval on the head
  else automatic mode
    SW->>VM: Final self-review<br/>fresh review agent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a new review agent, which took no part in the drafts or the earlier reviews, reads the PR head and its CI result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - findings go back to the author agent, which fixes them; the new head gets a new review
    VM-->>SW: Pass<br/>or findings
  end
  GW->>SW: Admit the merge step<br/>fresh token key name
  %%> When:
  %%> - manual mode: after the Gateway sees the approval on the exact head
  %%> - automatic mode: after the final self-review passes
  %%> - in both modes the PR's CI is green
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a token lives one hour and an approval can take longer, so the Gateway mints a new one for this step
  SW->>GH: Add to the merge queue<br/>enqueuePullRequest (App token)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Swamp adds the PR to the merge queue through GitHub's `enqueuePullRequest` GraphQL mutation, with the Gateway-minted App token passed by vault key name
  %%> - the Orbit App, through this Swamp step, decides whether the PR may merge; the merge queue then runs CI on the merge group and merges
  %%> History:
  %%> - GitHub auto-merge is no longer used
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - Swamp adding the PR to the merge queue; today the author runs `gh pr merge --auto` as `nckrtl` (the interim)
  %%> - the repository's auto-merge setting is switched off once Swamp enqueues PRs
  Note over GH: The queue and CI decide<br/>Required checks
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the merge queue lands the PR when `Required checks` pass
  SW-->>GW: Record the outcome<br/>command ready
  %%> Result:
  %%> - chart, page and cases are merged; the Gateway records the command as ready for the CLI and web
  %%> - building starts only now, with stage 2 onward
